| `scripts/expiring_tier.py` | The tier a gate test hands its findings to. In the template repository, which holds `copier.yml`, every finding is red. In a generated project a finding the baseline records warns until `expiring_tier.expires` and is red from that day, while an unrecorded finding, a copy over the recorded count, a line outside the `<file>:<line>: ` grammar and a baseline entry no finding matches are red at once. | imported by `tests/integration/test_config_reads_gate.py`, `tests/integration/test_exit_gate.py` and `scripts/record_gate_baseline.py` | [`expiring_tier.baseline`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`expiring_tier.expires`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Raises `TierError` and never ends the process. It finds nothing itself: each gate test finds its own lines. Not the writer of the baseline: `make gate-baseline` writes it. | [generate-and-upgrade.md](../guides/generate-and-upgrade.md) | always |
